# Unity CLI (GameForge) — routing

**Do not invent a second stack.** Primary = **Unity CLI + Pipeline** (`unity command` / `eval` / `test`). Optional = **`unity mcp`** (same Pipeline over Cursor stdio). Legacy assistant MCP = fallback only.

| Task | Use | Never use for this |
|------|-----|-------------------|
| Preflight / Safe Mode | `unity pipeline list --format json` | — |
| Scene / GO / asset **writes** | `unity command` (`open_scene`, `create_gameobject`, `batch`, `eval`, …) | Product `*Authoring` MenuItem scripts; human Hierarchy checklists |
| OVR read-back | `unity command eval` / `get_scene_hierarchy` | Blind `.unity` YAML edits |
| Save + compile poll | `unity command save_all` / `recompile` / `recompile_status` | — |
| **EditMode / PlayMode tests** | **`unity test`** or `POST /api/unity-cli/test` | **Test Runner MCP** |
| Play smoke | `unity command editor_play` | Play thrash loops |
| Screenshot | `unity command screenshot` | — |

`on_unavailable` means: **STOP** — do not ask the human to mount the scene manually. It does **not** forbid the agent from driving the live Editor via CLI.

Sidecar: `GET /api/unity-cli/preflight`, `POST /api/unity-cli/eval`, `/command`, `/test`.

Docs: `V57/docs/mcp/UNITY_CLI_INTEGRATIONS.md`, `UNITY_MCP_REQUIREMENT.md`.

**Do not** use `unity logs` for `Editor.log` — that is the CLI log. Use `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Unity\Editor\Editor.log` or console tools.

Policy: `agents.yaml` → `rules.unity_cli`, `rules.scene_authoring`, `run_unity_test_runner_via_cli: true`.
